No frame offset (-3..+3) aligns the streams, with or without the counters
excluded, so "one iteration out of phase" describes the ONSET, not the
consequence. MECHANISM: the replay's inputs are scheduled by FRAME; once
the main loop is one logic step out, every later input lands on a
different step and the match itself plays out differently.
=> NOT a class to ratify. This is a superset-invariant regression on
